  <h1>About the garden</h1>
  <p>Northfield started in 2016 on a lot behind the old library. There are forty raised beds, a tool shed, a rain barrel system and a compost corner that is mostly looked after by one very dedicated retired teacher.</p>
  <h2>Getting a plot</h2>
  <p>A plot costs $30 for the season and comes with water and the use of the shed. Plots are handed out in March from the waiting list, in the order people signed up.</p>
  <h2>Work mornings</h2>
  <p>We meet on the first Saturday of the month at nine. Bring gloves. Tea is provided.</p>
</main>
